Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Complex Numbers", "Section"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Off with your spell!", "Subsubsection",
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell["Off[General::spell];Off[General::spell1]", "Input",
  InitializationCell->True]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["For startup", "Subsubsection"],

Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["ComplexExpand",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  " seems to need time to start up and then runs faster the second time it is \
used."
}], "Text",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\(ComplexExpand[I]; \)\)], "Input",
  InitializationCell->True]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Normalization ", "Subsubsection",
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell["\<\
The following function normalizes non-zero complex numbers to unit \
length.\
\>", "Text",
  Evaluatable->False,
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(Norm[z_] := z\/Abs[z]\)], "Input",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["ComplexSimplify", "Subsubsection"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(ComplexSimplify[z_] := \(ComplexSimplify[{}]\)[z] /; Head[z] =!= List; 
    ComplexSimplify[vars_List] := 
      Function[z, \n\t\t
        Together[
            ComplexExpand[Re[z], vars, TargetFunctions \[Rule] {Re, Im}]] + \n
          \t\t\tTogether[
              ComplexExpand[Im[z], vars, TargetFunctions \[Rule] {Re, Im}]]\ 
            I]; \)], "Input",
  InitializationCell->True]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["ArgandPlot and RootPlot", "Subsubsection"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "This code for plotting complex numbers and complex roots was adapted from \
a Notebook ",
  StyleBox["Complex Roots  ",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  "by Dan Grayson and Paul C. Abbott."
}], "SmallText"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "The function ",
  StyleBox["ArgandPlot",
    FontFamily->"Courier",
    FontSize->10,
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  " plots a list of complex numbers in Cartesian coordinates.  The point size \
can be varied."
}], "Text"],

Cell["\<\
ArgandPlot[z_, w_:10, opts___Rule] := \t
        Show[Graphics[{AbsolutePointSize[w],
        Point /@ Transpose[{Re[z], Im[z]}] }],
        Axes->Automatic, AspectRatio->Automatic,
        AxesLabel->{\"Re\",\"Im\"},opts]\
\>", "Input",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell[TextData[{
  "The function ",
  StyleBox["RootPlot",
    FontFamily->"Courier",
    FontSize->10,
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  " plots the roots of a polynomial equation in the complex plane on an \
Argand diagram.  The point size can be varied."
}], "Text"],

Cell["\<\
RootPlot[eqn_, x_, w_:10,opts___Rule] := Module[{t},
         t = x /. N[Solve[eqn, x]] ;
         ArgandPlot[t,w,opts]]\
\>", "Input",
  InitializationCell->True]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["ComplexMap", "Subsubsection"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "The code envoked here is Copyright 1991 by Roman E. Maeder.  It has been \
adapted from Roman E. Maeder: ",
  StyleBox["Programming in Mathematica",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  ", Second Edition, Addison-Wesley, 1991.  A more detailed description and \
discussion of this package is given in the book ",
  StyleBox["Programming in Mathematica", "TI",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  ", Third Edition, by Roman E. Maeder. "
}], "SmallText",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell["\<\
With the distribution of the code it is stated: \"Permission is \
hereby granted to make copies of this file for any purpose other than direct \
profit, or as part of a commercial product, provided this copyright notice is \
left intact.  Sale, other than for the cost of media, is prohibited.  \
Permission is hereby granted to reproduce part or all of this file, provided \
that the source is acknowledged.  Enclosed with Mathematica by \
permission.\"\
\>", "SmallText",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell[TextData[{
  "To plot the graph of a complex\[Hyphen]valued function of a complex \
variable, four dimensions are required: two for the complex variable and two \
for the complex function value. One method to circumvent the need for four\
\[Hyphen]dimensional graphics is to show how the function transforms sets of \
lines that lie in the complex plane. Each line will be mapped into some curve \
in the complex plane and these can be represented in two dimensions. \nThe \
functions ",
  StyleBox["CartesianMap", "MR",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  " and ",
  StyleBox["PolarMap", "MR",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  " defined in this package make pictures of this form. ",
  StyleBox["CartesianMap", "MR",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  " shows the image of Cartesian coordinate lines while ",
  StyleBox["PolarMap", "MR",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  " shows the effect on polar coordinate lines. \nVersion 2.0 used the option \
PlotPoints to control the number of lines.  Now it uses the option Lines for \
this purpose. PlotPoints is used to control the quality of the lines, as it \
should be."
}], "SmallText",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell["Needs[\"Graphics`ComplexMap`\"];", "Input",
  InitializationCell->True,
  CellTags->"S5.33.1"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Arguments to colors", "Subsubsection"],

Cell["Needs[\"Graphics`ArgColors`\"];", "Input",
  InitializationCell->True]
}, Closed]]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Polynomials", "Section"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Cleaning up", "Subsubsection"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "This operation writes ",
  StyleBox["xyz",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "-polynomials or ",
  StyleBox["uvw",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "-polynomials in terms of monomials."
}], "Text",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\(Tidy[f_] := 
      Module[{$dummy}, 
        Plus@@MonomialList[f\ $dummy, {x, y, z, u, v, w}, 
              CoefficientDomain \[Rule] RationalFunctions] /. {$dummy \[Rule] 
              1}]; \)\)], "Input",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Unfortunately, ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox["MonomialList",
        FontWeight->"Bold"]]],
  " is an undocumented feature of ",
  StyleBox["Mathematica",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  ". It seems to have some bugs."
}], "Text"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Bases", "Subsubsection"],

Cell["", "Text",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell["\<\

Bxyz[nn_] := 
Sort[Flatten[Table[x^ii y^jj z^(nn-ii-jj),{ii,0,nn},{jj,0,nn-ii}]]]

Buvw[nn_] := 
Sort[Flatten[Table[u^ii v^jj w^(nn-ii-jj),{ii,0,nn},{jj,0,nn-ii}]]]
\
\>", "Input",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Dual variables", "Subsubsection"],

Cell["", "Text",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell["Dual[e_] := e /. {x->u, y->v, z->w, u->x, v->y, w->z};", "Input",
  InitializationCell->True]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Making assumptions about symbolic polynomials", "Subsubsection"],

Cell[BoxData[{
    \(\(ClearAll[SymQ]; \)\), 
    \(SymQ[x | y | z | u | v | w] := False\), 
    \(SymQ[HoldPattern[PD[a_, b_]]] := SymQ[a] || SymQ[b]\), 
    \(SymQ[HoldPattern[PE[a_, b_]]] := SymQ[a] || SymQ[b]\), 
    \(SymQ[HoldPattern[\(+a__\)]] := Or@@\(SymQ/@{a}\)\), 
    \(SymQ[HoldPattern[Times[a__]]] := Or@@\(SymQ/@{a}\)\), 
    \(SymQ[a_\^_] := SymQ[a]\), 
    \(SymQ[f_] := DegP[f] =!= 0\)}], "Input",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell[BoxData[{
    \(ClearAll[DeclaredSymQ]; \n
    DeclaredSymQ[f_Symbol] := 
      \((Hold[SymQ[f]] /. UpValues[f])\) === Hold[True]\), 
    \(DeclaredSymQ[f_\__] := 
      \((Hold[SymQ[f]] /. UpValues[f])\) === Hold[True]\), 
    \(DeclaredSymQ[_] := False\)}], "Input",
  InitializationCell->True]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Polynomial degree", "Subsubsection"],

Cell[BoxData[{
    \(\(ClearAll[DegP]; \)\), 
    \(\(DegP[x | y | z | u | v | w] := 1; \)\), 
    \(\(DegP[HoldPattern[PD[p_, q_]]] := Abs[DegP[p] - DegP[q]]; \)\), 
    \(\(DegP[HoldPattern[PE[p_, q_]]] := 1 /; DegP[p] == DegP[q] == 1; \)\), 
    \(\(DegP[p_Plus] := Max@@\(DegP/@\(List@@Expand[p]\)\); \)\), 
    \(\(DegP[p_Times] := Plus@@\(DegP/@\(List@@p\)\); \)\), 
    \(\(DegP[p_\^n_] := n\ DegP[p]; \)\), 
    \(DegP[f_] := 0 /; \(\[InvisibleSpace]\(! \((DeclaredSymQ[f])\)\)\)\)}], 
  "Input",
  InitializationCell->True]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
  "An isomorphism from ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(\[DoubleStruckCapitalC][u, v, w]\)]],
  " to  ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(\[DoubleStruckCapitalC][
        \[PartialD]\_x\(, \[PartialD]\_y\(, \[PartialD]\_z\)\)]\)]],
  " "
}], "Subsubsection"],

Cell["", "Text",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell["\<\

PolyToDiff[u^(n_.)] := Function[p, D[p, {x, n}]]; 

PolyToDiff[v^(n_.)] := Function[p, D[p, {y, n}]]; 

PolyToDiff[w^(n_.)] := Function[p, D[p, {z, n}]]; 

PolyToDiff[u^(n_.)*v^(m_.)] := 
   Function[p,D[p,{x,n},{y,m}]]; 
   
PolyToDiff[u^(n_.)*w^(m_.)] := 
   Function[p,D[p,{x,n},{z,m}]]; 
   
PolyToDiff[v^(n_.)*w^(m_.)] := 
   Function[p,D[p,{y,n},{z,m}]]; 
   
PolyToDiff[u^(k_.)*v^(m_.)*w^(n_.)] := 
   Function[p,D[p,{x,k},{y,m},{z,n}]];
\
\>", "Input",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell["", "Text",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell["PolyToDiff[f_] := Function[p, f*p] /; FreeQ[f, u|v|w];", "Input",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell["", "Text",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell["\<\

PolyToDiff[(f_)+(g_)] := 
  Function[p, PolyToDiff[f][p] + PolyToDiff[g][p]]
\
\>", "Input",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell["", "Text",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell["\<\

PolyToDiff[(f_)^(n_)] := 
  Function[p, Nest[PolyToDiff[f], p, n]]
\
\>", "Input",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell["", "Text",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell["\<\

PolyToDiff[(f_)*(g_)] := 
  Composition[PolyToDiff[f], PolyToDiff[g]]
\
\>", "Input",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell["", "Text",
  InitializationCell->True]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Implementation of polydifferentiation", "Subsubsection"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "If  ",
  StyleBox["DegP[q]<DegP[p]", "InlineInput"],
  " then we are differentiating ",
  StyleBox["q", "InlineInput"],
  " with respect to ",
  StyleBox["p", "InlineInput"],
  ".",
  StyleBox[" ", "InlineInput"],
  "If  ",
  StyleBox["DegP[p]<DegP[q]", "InlineInput"],
  " then we are differentiating ",
  StyleBox["p", "InlineInput"],
  " with respect to ",
  StyleBox["q", "InlineInput"],
  ".",
  StyleBox[" ", "InlineInput"],
  "If we know that neither ",
  StyleBox["p", "InlineInput"],
  " nor ",
  StyleBox["q", "InlineInput"],
  " contain any symbolic parts, then we can compute the result. The following \
 is the main optimization\[LongDash]if we know that we can compute the final  \
result, then we pass the job to  ",
  StyleBox["PolyToDiff", "InlineInput"],
  "."
}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\(ClearAll[PD]; \)\)], "Input",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(PD[p_, q_] := 
      \(PolyToDiff[q]\)[p]\  /; 
        \[InvisibleSpace]\(! \((SymQ[p])\)\) && 
          \(\[InvisibleSpace]\(! \((SymQ[q])\)\)\) && 
          DegP[p] \[GreaterEqual] DegP[q]; \n\n
    PD[p_, q_] := 
      Dual[\(PolyToDiff[Dual[p]]\)[Dual[q]]]\  /; 
        \[InvisibleSpace]\(! \((SymQ[p])\)\) && 
          \(\[InvisibleSpace]\(! \((SymQ[q])\)\)\) && 
          DegP[q] \[GreaterEqual] DegP[p]; \)], "Input",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell["Additivity:", "Text",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],

Cell[BoxData[{
    \(\(PD[p_Plus, q_] := \((PD[#1, q]&)\)/@p; \)\), 
    \(\(PD[p_, q_Plus] := \((PD[p, #1]&)\)/@q; \)\)}], "Input",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell["Homogeneity :", "Text",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],

Cell[BoxData[{
    \(PD[a_\ p_. , q_] := a\ PD[p, q] /; a =!= 1 && DegP[a] == 0\), 
    \(\(PD[p_, a_\ q_. ] := a\ PD[p, q] /; a =!= 1 && DegP[a] == 0; \)\)}], 
  "Input",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["Associative properties of ",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  StyleBox["PD", "Program",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  StyleBox[":",
    FontWeight->"Bold"]
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Rules for the case when one of the arguments is a product. We nest ",
  StyleBox["PD", "InlineInput"],
  " in such a way that differentiation with respect to symbolic polynomials  \
is on the outside. This way the inner ",
  StyleBox["PD", "InlineInput"],
  "'s can be evaluated."
}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[{
    \(\(PD[p_, q_\ r_] := 
      PD[PD[p, q], r] /; DegP[p] \[GreaterEqual] DegP[q\ r]; \)\), 
    \(\(PD[p_, q_\^n_] := 
      Nest[PD[#1, q]&, p, n] /; DegP[p] \[GreaterEqual] DegP[q\^n]; \)\), 
    \(\(PD[p_\ q_, r_] := 
      PD[p, PD[q, r]] /; DegP[r] \[GreaterEqual] DegP[p\ q]; \)\), 
    \(\(PD[p_\^n_, q_] := 
      Nest[PD[p, #1]&, q, n] /; DegP[q] \[GreaterEqual] DegP[p\^n]; \)\)}], 
  "Input",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["Derivative properties of ",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  StyleBox["PD", "Program",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  StyleBox[":",
    FontWeight->"Bold"]
}], "Text"],

Cell["Special rules apply when one of the factors has degree one:", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(PD[p_, q_] := p\ q /; DegP[q] == 0 || DegP[p] == 0\)], "Input",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(PD[p_\ q_, r_] := 
      p\ PD[q, r] + q\ PD[p, r] /; 1 == DegP[r] \[LessEqual] DegP[p\ q]; 
    PD[p_\^n_, q_] := 
      n\ p\^\(n - 1\)\ PD[p, q] /; 1 == DegP[q] \[LessEqual] DegP[p\^n]; \)], 
  "Input",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell[BoxData[{
    \(\(PD[p_, q_\ r_] := 
      q\ PD[p, r] + r\ PD[p, q] /; 1 == DegP[p] \[LessEqual] DegP[q\ r]; 
    \)\), 
    \(\(PD[p_, q_\^n_] := 
      n\ q\^\(n - 1\)\ PD[p, q] /; 1 == DegP[p] \[LessEqual] DegP[q\^n]; 
    \)\)}], "Input",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["Commutative properties of ",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  StyleBox["PD", "Program",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  StyleBox[":",
    FontWeight->"Bold"]
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Rules that reorder nested ",
  StyleBox["PD", "InlineInput"],
  "'s into a canonical order. Non-symbolic second arguments are pushed  \
inside, symbolic arguments are ordered in a canonical order. The role of ",
  " HoldPattern",
  " in the pattern below is to prevent evaluation of ",
  StyleBox["PD", "InlineInput"],
  " that occurs in the pattern."
}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(PD[HoldPattern[PD[p_, q_]], r_] := 
      PD[PD[p, r], q] /; SymQ[q] && \[InvisibleSpace]\(! \((SymQ[r])\)\); \n\n
    PD[HoldPattern[PD[p_, q_]], r_] := 
      PD[PD[p, r], q] /; Order[q, r] == \(-1\) && SymQ[q] && SymQ[r]; \n\n
    PD[HoldPattern[PD[p_, q_]], r_] := 
      PD[PD[p, r], q] /; \n\t\t
        Order[q, r] == \(-1\) && \(\[InvisibleSpace]\(! \((SymQ[q])\)\)\) && 
          \(\[InvisibleSpace]\(! \((SymQ[r])\)\)\); \)], "Input",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell[BoxData[{
    \(\(PD[p_, HoldPattern[PD[q_, r_]]] := 
      PD[q, PD[p, r]] /; SymQ[q] && \(\[InvisibleSpace]\(! \((SymQ[p])\)\)\); 
    \)\), 
    \(\(PD[p_, HoldPattern[PD[q_, r_]]] := 
      PD[q, PD[p, r]] /; Order[p, q] == \(-1\) && SymQ[q] && SymQ[p]; \)\), 
    \(\(PD[p_, HoldPattern[PD[q_, r_]]] := 
      PD[q, PD[p, r]] /; 
        Order[p, q] == \(-1\) && \(\[InvisibleSpace]\(! \((SymQ[q])\)\)\) && 
          \(\[InvisibleSpace]\(! \((SymQ[p])\)\)\); \)\)}], "Input",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Triple products",
  FontWeight->"Bold"]], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "These rules concern ",
  StyleBox["collinear points",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " and ",
  StyleBox["concurrent lines",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  ". "
}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(PD[HoldPattern[PE[p_, q_]], r_] := 
      0 /; \ PE[p, r] == 0 || PE[q, r] == 0; \n
    PD[r_, HoldPattern[PE[p_, q_]]] := 0 /; \ PE[p, r] == 0 || PE[q, r] == 0; 
    \)], "Input",
  InitializationCell->True]
}, Closed]]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Lines and Points", "Section"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["An incidence matrix", "Subsubsection",
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell["The incidence matrix of configuration of lines and points ", "Text",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True,
  FontWeight->"Bold"],

Cell["\<\
MI[ll_,pp_] := Outer[If[N[Expand[PD[#1,#2]] == 0],1,0]&,ll,pp]\
\>",
   "Input",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Exterior product", "Subsubsection",
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell["Making exterior product a multilinear operation", "Text",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True,
  FontWeight->"Bold"],

Cell["\<\
PE[p___, 0, q___]       := 0;
PE[p___, l_ + m_, q___] := PE[p,l,q] + PE[p,m,q];
PE[p___, n_ l_, q___]   := n PE[p,l,q]/; DegP[n] == 0;\
\>", "Input",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell["Making exterior product a skew-symmetric operation", "Text",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True,
  FontWeight->"Bold"],

Cell["PE[p___, l_,l_, q___] := 0;", "Input",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell["PE[p___, l_,m_, q___] := -PE[p,m,l,q] /; Order[l,m] == -1; ", "Input",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell["Exterior products of lines are points ", "Text",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True,
  FontWeight->"Bold"],

Cell["PE[x,y] :=  w; PE[x,z] := -v; PE[y,z] :=  u; ", "Input",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell["Exterior products of points are lines", "Text",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True,
  FontWeight->"Bold"],

Cell["PE[u,v] :=  z; PE[u,w] := -y; PE[v,w] :=  x;", "Input",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell["Exterior product applied to a sequence pair by pair", "Text",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True,
  FontWeight->"Bold"],

Cell["PES[v_] := Apply[PE,Partition[Append[v,First[v]],2,1],{1}];", "Input",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["ImplicitPlot", "Subsubsection"],

Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["ImplicitPlot[eqn,{x,a,b}] ",
    FontFamily->"Courier",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "draws a graph of the set of points that satisfy the equation ",
  StyleBox["eqn",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  ".  The variable ",
  StyleBox["x",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  " is associated with the horizontal axis and ranges from ",
  StyleBox["a",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  " to ",
  StyleBox["b",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  ".  The remaining variable in the equation is associated with the vertical \
axis. "
}], "Text",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["ImplicitPlot[eqn, {x, a, x1, x2, ..., b}]",
    FontFamily->"Courier",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  " allows the user to specify values of ",
  StyleBox["x",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  " where special care must be exercised. "
}], "Text",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["ImplicitPlot[{eqn1, eqn2, ...}, {x, a, b}] ",
    FontFamily->"Courier",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "allows more than one equation to be plotted, with ",
  StyleBox["PlotStyles",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  " set as in the ",
  StyleBox["Plot",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  " function. "
}], "Text",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["ImplicitPlot[eqn, {x, a, b}, {y, a, b}] ",
    FontFamily->"Courier",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "uses a ",
  StyleBox["contour plot",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " method of generating the plot.  This form does not allow specification of \
intermediate points."
}], "Text",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell["Needs[\"Graphics`ImplicitPlot`\"];", "Input",
  InitializationCell->True]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Colors", "Subsubsection"],

Cell["<<Graphics`Colors`", "Input",
  InitializationCell->True]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Drawing Points and Lines", "Subsubsection",
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell["A program by Marko Petkovsek (modified slightly by Scott)", "Text",
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell["The command", "Text",
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell["Draw[ list,  From->{A1, A2, A3, p},  To->{B1, B2, B3, q} ]  ", "Input",
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell[TextData[{
  "draws the points and lines listed in list, as they are seen in the plane  \
",
  StyleBox["z == 1",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  ".  "
}], "Text",
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell[TextData[{
  "An element of list can be a linear form in either ",
  StyleBox["u",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  ", ",
  StyleBox["v",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  ", ",
  StyleBox["w",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "  or  ",
  StyleBox["x",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  ", ",
  StyleBox["y",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  ", ",
  StyleBox["z",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  ",   or a list consisting of a form and a string (to be used as a label for \
that element in the picture).   The ordering within list is not important."
}], "Text",
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell["\<\
The points are rendered in black, and the lines are rendered in \
blue.   Points at infinity are drawn as dotted lines through the origin \
representing directions, and line at infinity is drawn as a dashed square \
frame around the whole picture.  \
\>", "Text",
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell["\<\
The Plot Range contains all the given points, the origin, points \
closest to the origin on each of the given lines, and all finite \
intersections of the given lines among themselves and also with the \
coordinate axes. \
\>", "Text",
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell[TextData[{
  "The values of the two optional arguments,  From  and  To ,  must be lists \
of three points and one line, both representing a nondegenerate \
configuration.    Before anything else,  the points and lines given in  list  \
are transformed using a projective transformation which maps  ",
  StyleBox["Ai",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "  to  ",
  StyleBox["Bi",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "  and  ",
  StyleBox["p",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  " to  ",
  StyleBox["q",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  " .   The default value for both optional arguments is ",
  StyleBox["{w,  u + w,  v + w,  z}",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  ".    So, for example,  omitting  To  results in mapping the points and the \
line given in  From  to the origin, the two unit points, and the line at \
infinity,  respectively; while omitting both arguments specifies the identity \
transformation."
}], "Text",
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell["\<\
Draw1  is just like  Draw  except that it uses a circular (rather \
than square) frame for the line at infinity.\
\>", "Text",
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell["\<\
Options[Draw] := {From -> {w,u+w,v+w,z}, To -> {w,u+w,v+w,z}};

Draw[l_List, opts___] :=

    Module[{ll = If[Head[#] === List, #, {#,\"\"}]& /@ l,
            mm, points, lines, allLines, intersections, 
            finPoints, infPoints, finIntersections,
            finLines, affPoints, affIntersections, 
            affDirections, affLines, closest, allPoints,
            xList, yList, minX, maxX, minY, maxY,
            width, heigth, infLine, frame, pointLabels,
            lineLabels, directionLabels, frameLabel, lp,
            ref1, ref2, size },
            
        ref1 = From /. {opts} /. Options[Draw];
        ref2 = To /. {opts} /. Options[Draw];
        mm = MQL[Join[PES[Drop[ref1,-1]], {Last[ref1]}],
                 Join[PES[Drop[ref2,-1]], {Last[ref2]}] ];
        points = Select[ll,!(FreeQ[#,u] && FreeQ[#,v] && FreeQ[#,w]) &];
        lines  = Select[ll,!(FreeQ[#,x] && FreeQ[#,y] && FreeQ[#,z]) &];
        points = {TP[mm][#[[1]]], #[[2]]}& /@ points;
        lines =  {TL[mm][#[[1]]], #[[2]]}& /@ lines;
        allLines = Union[#[[1]]& /@ lines, {x, y}];
        intersections = PE @@ # & /@ 
            Select[Sort /@ Join @@ Outer[List, allLines, allLines] 
            // Union, #[[1]] =!= #[[2]] &];
        finPoints = Select[points, Coefficient[#[[1]], w] =!= 0 &];
        infPoints = Select[points, Coefficient[#[[1]], w] === 0 &];
        finIntersections = Select[intersections,
            Coefficient[#, w] =!= 0 &];
        finLines = Select[lines, 
            !(Coefficient[#[[1]],x] === Coefficient[#[[1]],y] === 0) &];
        infLine = Select[lines, 
             (Coefficient[#[[1]],x] === Coefficient[#[[1]],y] === 0) &];
        If[Length[infLine] > 1, infLine = First[infLine]];                 
        pointLabels = #[[2]]& /@ finPoints;
        affPoints = 
            {Coefficient[#[[1]],u], Coefficient[#[[1]],v]}/
             Coefficient[#[[1]],w] & /@ finPoints;
        affIntersections = 
            {Coefficient[#,u], Coefficient[#,v]}/Coefficient[#,w] & /@
             finIntersections;
        directionLabels = #[[2]]& /@ infPoints;
        affDirections = (Coefficient[#,v] x - Coefficient[#,u] y == 0
            )& /@ infPoints;
        lineLabels = #[[2]]& /@ finLines;
        affLines = Thread[((#[[1]]& /@ finLines) /. z->1) == 0];
        closest = -{Coefficient[#[[1]],x], Coefficient[#[[1]],y]
           } Coefficient[#[[1]],z]/(Coefficient[#[[1]],x]^2 + 
            Coefficient[#[[1]],y]^2) & /@ finLines;
        allPoints = Join[affPoints, affIntersections, closest, {{0,0}}];
        xList = First /@ allPoints;
        yList = Last /@ allPoints;
        minX = Min[xList];
        maxX = Max[xList];
        minY = Min[yList];
        maxY = Max[yList];
        width = maxX - minX;
        height = maxY - minY;
        If[width == height == 0, width = height = 2; 
            minX = minY = -1; maxX = maxY = 1];
        size = Max[width, height];
        {minX, maxX} = {minX, maxX} + 
            ((size - width)/2 + size/10){-1,1};
        {minY, maxY} = {minY, maxY} +
            ((size - height)/2 + size/10){-1,1};
        affLines = Line /@ 
            (Clip[#, minX, maxX, minY, maxY]& /@ affLines);
        lineLabels = Text @@ # & /@
            Thread[{lineLabels, lp = 
            #[[1,1]]& /@ affLines,
            Where[#, minX, maxX, minY, maxY]& /@ lp}];
        affDirections = Line /@ 
            (Clip[#, minX, maxX, minY, maxY]& /@ affDirections);
        directionLabels = Text @@ # & /@
            Thread[{directionLabels, lp = 
            #[[1,2]]& /@ affDirections,
            Where[#, minX, maxX, minY, maxY]& /@ lp}];
        affPoints = Point /@ affPoints;
        pointLabels = Text @@ # & /@ 
            Thread[{pointLabels, lp = #[[1]]& /@ affPoints, 
            Where[#, minX, maxX, minY, maxY]& /@ lp}];
        If[infLine === {},
            frame = {}; frameLabel = {},
            frame = {Line[{{minX,minY},{maxX,minY},{maxX,maxY},
                {minX,maxY},{minX,minY}} ]}; 
                 frameLabel = {Text[infLine[[1,2]],
                     {(minX + maxX)/2, minY}, SS] } ];
        Show[Graphics[Join[
           {PointSize[0.02], RGBColor[0,0,0]},
            affPoints,
           {Thickness[0.003], RGBColor[0,0,1]},
            affLines,
           {RGBColor[0,0,0]},
            pointLabels, directionLabels,
           {RGBColor[0,0,1]},
            lineLabels, frameLabel,
           {Thickness[0.0075], Dashing[{0.025,0.025}], RGBColor[0,0,1]},
            frame,
           {Thickness[0.005], Dashing[{0.005,0.02}], RGBColor[0,0,0]},
            affDirections ] ],
                AspectRatio -> Automatic,
                PlotRange -> {{minX, maxX} + 0.2 size {-1,1}, 
                    {minY, maxY} + 0.2 size {-1,1}},
                DisplayFunction -> $DisplayFunction,
                Axes -> None,
                Ticks -> None,
                DefaultFont -> {\"Courier\", 12}] ];
        
        
displ = 1.75;
NN = displ {0,-1}; SS = -NN; EE = displ {-1,0}; WW = -EE;
NE = NN + EE; SE = SS + EE; NW = NN + WW; SW = SS + WW;



Clip[line_, minX_, maxX_, minY_, maxY_] :=
        Select[{x,y} /.# & /@ (First /@ 
            Select[Solve[Append[{line},#], {x,y}]& /@ 
           {x == maxX, y == maxY, y == minY, x == minX},
           (# =!= {})&]), (minX <= #[[1]] <= maxX && 
            minY <= #[[2]] <= maxY)&] // Union;
            
            
Where[{x_,y_}, minX_, maxX_, minY_, maxY_] :=
        Which[x == minX && y == minY, NE,
              x == maxX && y == minY, NW,
              x == maxX && y == maxY, SW,
              x == minX && y == maxY, SE,
              x == minX, EE,
              x == maxX, WW,
              y == minY, NN,
              y == maxY, SS,
              True, SE];
            

Options[Draw1] := {From -> {w,u+w,v+w,z}, To -> {w,u+w,v+w,z}};

Draw1[l_List, opts___] :=

    Module[{ll = If[Head[#] === List, #, {#,\"\"}]& /@ l,
            mm, points, lines, allLines, intersections, 
            finPoints, infPoints, finIntersections,
            finLines, affPoints, affIntersections, 
            affDirections, affLines, closest, allPoints,
            xList, yList, minX, maxX, minY, maxY,
            width, heigth, infLine, frame, pointLabels,
            lineLabels, directionLabels, frameLabel, lp,
            ref1, ref2, center, radius, pr },
            
        ref1 = From /. {opts} /. Options[Draw];
        ref2 = To /. {opts} /. Options[Draw];
        mm = MQL[Join[PES[Drop[ref1,-1]], {Last[ref1]}],
                 Join[PES[Drop[ref2,-1]], {Last[ref2]}] ];
        points = Select[ll,!(FreeQ[#,u] && FreeQ[#,v] && FreeQ[#,w]) &];
        lines  = Select[ll,!(FreeQ[#,x] && FreeQ[#,y] && FreeQ[#,z]) &];
        points = {TP[mm][#[[1]]], #[[2]]}& /@ points;
        lines =  {TL[mm][#[[1]]], #[[2]]}& /@ lines;
        allLines = Union[#[[1]]& /@ lines, {x, y}];
        intersections = PE @@ # & /@ 
            Select[Sort /@ Join @@ Outer[List, allLines, allLines] 
            // Union, #[[1]] =!= #[[2]] &];
        finPoints = Select[points, Coefficient[#[[1]], w] =!= 0 &];
        infPoints = Select[points, Coefficient[#[[1]], w] === 0 &];
        finIntersections = Select[intersections,
            Coefficient[#, w] =!= 0 &];
        finLines = Select[lines, 
            !(Coefficient[#[[1]],x] === Coefficient[#[[1]],y] === 0) &];
        infLine = Select[lines, 
             (Coefficient[#[[1]],x] === Coefficient[#[[1]],y] === 0) &];
        If[Length[infLine] > 1, infLine = First[infLine]];                 
        pointLabels = #[[2]]& /@ finPoints;
        affPoints = 
            {Coefficient[#[[1]],u], Coefficient[#[[1]],v]}/
             Coefficient[#[[1]],w] & /@ finPoints;
        affIntersections = 
            {Coefficient[#,u], Coefficient[#,v]}/Coefficient[#,w] & /@
             finIntersections;
        directionLabels = #[[2]]& /@ infPoints;
        affDirections = (Coefficient[#,v] x - Coefficient[#,u] y == 0
            )& /@ infPoints;
        lineLabels = #[[2]]& /@ finLines;
        affLines = Thread[((#[[1]]& /@ finLines) /. z->1) == 0];
        closest = -{Coefficient[#[[1]],x], Coefficient[#[[1]],y]
           } Coefficient[#[[1]],z]/(Coefficient[#[[1]],x]^2 + 
            Coefficient[#[[1]],y]^2) & /@ finLines;
        allPoints = Join[affPoints, affIntersections, closest, {{0,0}}];
        xList = First /@ allPoints;
        yList = Last /@ allPoints;
        minX = Min[xList];
        maxX = Max[xList];
        minY = Min[yList];
        maxY = Max[yList];
        width = maxX - minX;
        height = maxY - minY;
        If[width == height == 0, width = height = 2; 
            minX = minY = -1; maxX = maxY = 1];
        center = {(minX + maxX)/2, (minY + maxY)/2};
        radius = 1.1 Sqrt[width^2 + height^2]/2 //N;
        affLines = Line /@ 
            (Clip1[#, center, radius]& /@ affLines);
        lineLabels = Text @@ # & /@
            Thread[{lineLabels, lp = 
            #[[1,1]]& /@ affLines,
            Where1[#, center, displ]& /@ lp}];
        affDirections = Line /@ 
            (Clip1[#, center, radius]& /@ affDirections);
        directionLabels = Text @@ # & /@
            Thread[{directionLabels, lp = 
            #[[1,2]]& /@ affDirections,
            Where1[#, center, displ]& /@ lp}];
        affPoints = Point /@ affPoints;
        pointLabels = Text @@ # & /@ 
            Thread[{pointLabels, lp = #[[1]]& /@ affPoints, 
            Where1[#, center, displ]& /@ lp}];
        If[infLine === {},
            frame = {}; frameLabel = {},
            frame = {Circle[center, radius]}; 
                 frameLabel = {Text[infLine[[1,2]],
                     center - {0, radius}, SS] } ];
        pr = (1.1 radius {-1,1} + #)& /@ center;
        Show[Graphics[Join[
           {PointSize[0.03], RGBColor[0,0,0]},
            affPoints,
           {Thickness[0.0075], RGBColor[0,0,1]},
            affLines,
           {RGBColor[0,0,0]},
            pointLabels, directionLabels,
           {RGBColor[0,0,1]},
            lineLabels, frameLabel,
           {Thickness[0.0075], Dashing[{0.025,0.025}], RGBColor[0,0,1]},
            frame,
           {Thickness[0.0075], Dashing[{0.005,0.02}], RGBColor[0,0,0]},
            affDirections ] ],
                AspectRatio -> Automatic,
                PlotRange -> pr,
                DisplayFunction -> $DisplayFunction,
                Axes -> Automatic,
                Ticks -> None] ];
        
        
Clip1[line_, center_, radius_] :=
    {x,y} /. Solve[{line, 
        (Plus @@ (({x,y} - center)^2)) == radius^2}, {x,y} ]; 
            
            
Where1[{x_,y_}, center_, displ_] :=
    Block[{rx, ry},
        {rx, ry} = {x,y} - center;
        If[{rx, ry} != {0, 0},
           {rx, ry} / Sqrt[rx^2 + ry^2] displ // N,
            SE ]];
        
            

\
\>", "Input",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True]
}, Closed]]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Transformations and coordinates", "Section"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Mappings of forms, quadrangles and quadrilaterals", "Subsubsection",
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell["\<\
Given the matrix of coordinates of a point transformation, to find \
the corresponding mapping of polynomials\
\>", "Text",
  AspectRatioFixed->True,
  FontWeight->"Bold"],

Cell[BoxData[{
    \(TP[m_] := \n\tTidy[#1 /. Thread[{u, v, w} \[Rule] m . {u, v, w}]]&; \n
    \(TL[m_] := 
      Tidy[#1 /. Thread[{x, y, z} \[Rule] {x, y, z} . Inverse[m]]]&; \)\), 
    \(\(QTL[m_] := 
      Tidy[#1 /. Thread[{x, y, z} \[Rule] {x, y, z} . QuasiInverse[m]]]&; 
    \)\)}], "Input",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell["\<\
Producing vectors and matrices of coordinates from points and lines\
\
\>", "Text",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True,
  FontWeight->"Bold"],

Cell["\<\
CP[p_] := Apply[PD,{{x,p},{y,p},{z,p}},{1}];

CL[l_] := Apply[PD,{{l,u},{l,v},{l,w}},{1}];

MP[s_] := Map[CP,s];
\t\t\t\t\t\t  
ML[s_] := Map[CL,s];\
\>", "Input",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell["Mapping quadrangles and quadrilaterals", "Text",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True,
  FontWeight->"Bold"],

Cell["\<\
MQP[q_, r_] := Module[{mm,vv,nn,oo,ww,pp},
\tmm = MP[q[[{1,2,3}]]];
\tvv = CP[q[[4]]] . Inverse[mm];
\tnn = {{vv[[1]],0,0},{0,vv[[2]],0},{0,0,vv[[3]]}} . mm;
\too = MP[r[[{1,2,3}]]];
\tww = CP[r[[4]]] . Inverse[oo];
\tpp = {{ww[[1]],0,0},{0,ww[[2]],0},{0,0,ww[[3]]}} . oo;
 Simplify[Inverse[nn] . pp]];\
\>", "Input",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell["\<\
MQL[q_, r_] := Module[{mm,vv,nn,oo,ww,pp},
\tmm = ML[q[[{1,2,3}]]];
\tvv = CL[q[[4]]] . Inverse[mm];
\tnn = {{vv[[1]],0,0},{0,vv[[2]],0},{0,0,vv[[3]]}} . mm;
\too = ML[r[[{1,2,3}]]];
\tww = CL[r[[4]]] . Inverse[oo];
\tpp = {{ww[[1]],0,0},{0,ww[[2]],0},{0,0,ww[[3]]}} . oo;
 Simplify[Transpose[nn] . Inverse[Transpose[pp]]]];\
\>", "Input",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Crossratios", "Subsubsection",
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell["Crossratio of four points on a line", "Text",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True,
  FontWeight->"Bold"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(ClearAll[RP, RL]\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(RP[AA_, BB_, CC_, DD_] := 
      Module[{mm, ac, bc, ad, bd, sc, sd}, mm = MP[{AA, BB, CC, DD}]; \n\t\t
        If[Expand[PE[AA, BB]] === 0 || \n\t\t\t\t\ \ \ 
            Expand[PE[BB, CC]] === 0 || \ \ \n\t\t\t\t\ \ \ 
            Expand[PE[AA, CC]] === 0 || \ \ \n\t\t\t\t\ \ \ 
            Expand[PD[PE[AA, BB], CC]] =!= 0 || \n\t\t\t\ \ \ \ \ 
            Expand[PD[PE[AA, BB], DD]] =!= 0, "\<Error\>", \n\t\t\t
          sc = \(Solve[
                mm\[LeftDoubleBracket]3\[RightDoubleBracket] == 
                  ac\ mm\[LeftDoubleBracket]1\[RightDoubleBracket] + 
                    bc\ mm\[LeftDoubleBracket]2\[RightDoubleBracket], {ac, 
                  bc}]\)\[LeftDoubleBracket]1\[RightDoubleBracket]; 
          sd = \(Solve[
                mm\[LeftDoubleBracket]4\[RightDoubleBracket] == 
                  ad\ mm\[LeftDoubleBracket]1\[RightDoubleBracket] + 
                    bd\ mm\[LeftDoubleBracket]2\[RightDoubleBracket], {ad, 
                  bd}]\)\[LeftDoubleBracket]1\[RightDoubleBracket]; 
          Simplify[\(\(ad\ bc\)\/\(bd\ ac\) /. sc\) /. sd]]]\)], "Input",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell["Crossratio of four lines in a pencil", "Text",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True,
  FontWeight->"Bold"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(RL[AA_, BB_, CC_, DD_] := 
      Module[{mm, ac, bc, ad, bd, sc, sd}, mm = ML[{AA, BB, CC, DD}]; \t\n\t\t
        If[Expand[PE[AA, BB]] === 0 || \n\t\t\t\t\ \ \ 
            Expand[PE[BB, CC]] === 0 || \ \ \n\t\t\t\t\ \ \ 
            Expand[PE[AA, CC]] === 0 || \ \ \n\t\t\t\t\ \ \ 
            Expand[PD[CC, PE[AA, BB]]] =!= 0 || \n\t\t\t\ \ \ \ \ 
            Expand[PD[DD, PE[AA, BB]]] =!= 0, "\<Error\>", 
          sc = \(Solve[
                mm\[LeftDoubleBracket]3\[RightDoubleBracket] == 
                  ac\ mm\[LeftDoubleBracket]1\[RightDoubleBracket] + 
                    bc\ mm\[LeftDoubleBracket]2\[RightDoubleBracket], {ac, 
                  bc}]\)\[LeftDoubleBracket]1\[RightDoubleBracket]; 
          sd = \(Solve[
                mm\[LeftDoubleBracket]4\[RightDoubleBracket] == 
                  ad\ mm\[LeftDoubleBracket]1\[RightDoubleBracket] + 
                    bd\ mm\[LeftDoubleBracket]2\[RightDoubleBracket], {ad, 
                  bd}]\)\[LeftDoubleBracket]1\[RightDoubleBracket]; 
          Simplify[\(\(ad\ bc\)\/\(bd\ ac\) /. sc\) /. sd]]]\)], "Input",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Positioning via  relative coordinates", "Subsubsection",
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell["Positioning a fourth point on a line", "Text",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True,
  FontWeight->"Bold"],

Cell["ClearAll[XP,XL]", "Input",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell[BoxData[{
    \(\(XP[AA_, BB_, CC_, 0, 0] := 0\/0; \)\), 
    \(XP[AA_, BB_, CC_, ad_, bd_] := 
      Module[{mm, ac, bc, sc}, mm = MP[{AA, BB, CC}]; \n\t\t
        If[Expand[PE[AA, BB]] === 0 || \n\t\t\t\tExpand[PE[BB, CC]] === 0 || 
            \n\t\t\t\tExpand[PE[AA, CC]] === 0 || 
            Expand[PD[PE[AA, BB], CC]] =!= 0, "\<Error\>", 
          sc = \(Solve[
                mm\[LeftDoubleBracket]3\[RightDoubleBracket] == 
                  ac\ mm\[LeftDoubleBracket]1\[RightDoubleBracket] + 
                    bc\ mm\[LeftDoubleBracket]2\[RightDoubleBracket], {ac, 
                  bc}]\)\[LeftDoubleBracket]1\[RightDoubleBracket]; 
          Tidy[Simplify[ac\ ad\ AA + bc\ bd\ BB /. sc]]]]; 
    XP[AA_, BB_, CC_, ComplexInfinity] := AA; 
    XP[AA_, BB_, CC_, ad_] := XP[AA, BB, CC, ad, 1]; \)}], "Input",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell["Positioning a fourth line in a pencil", "Text",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True,
  FontWeight->"Bold"],

Cell[BoxData[{
    \(\(XL[AA_, BB_, CC_, 0, 0] := 0\/0; \)\), 
    \(XL[AA_, BB_, CC_, ad_, bd_] := 
      Module[{mm, ac, bc, sc}, mm = ML[{AA, BB, CC}]; \t\t\n\t\t
        If[Expand[PE[AA, BB]] === 0 || \n\t\t\t\tExpand[PE[BB, CC]] === 0 || 
            \n\t\t\t\tExpand[PE[AA, CC]] === 0 || 
            Expand[PD[CC, PE[AA, BB]]] =!= 0, "\<Error\>", 
          sc = \(Solve[
                mm\[LeftDoubleBracket]3\[RightDoubleBracket] == 
                  ac\ mm\[LeftDoubleBracket]1\[RightDoubleBracket] + 
                    bc\ mm\[LeftDoubleBracket]2\[RightDoubleBracket], {ac, 
                  bc}]\)\[LeftDoubleBracket]1\[RightDoubleBracket]; 
          Tidy[Simplify[ac\ ad\ AA + bc\ bd\ BB /. sc]]]]; \n
    XL[AA_, BB_, CC_, ComplexInfinity] := AA; \n
    \(XL[AA_, BB_, CC_, ad_] := XL[AA, BB, CC, ad, 1]; \)\)}], "Input",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Some Euclidean constructions", "Subsubsection"],

Cell["Dropping a perpendicular from a point to a line.", "Text",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(Perp[p_, l_] := 
      Tidy[PE[p, \ \(TP[{{0, 1, 0}, {\(-1\), 0, 0}, {0, 0, 1}}]\)[PE[l, z]]]]
        \)], "Input",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell["The matrix for perpendicular reflection about a line.", "Text",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\(Refl[l_] := 
      \((MQP[{u + I\ v, u - I\ v, #1, #2}, \n
              \t\t\t\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]{u - I\ v, u + I\ v, #1, #2}]&)\)@@
        \(({PE[l, PE[u + I\ v, #]], PE[l, PE[u - I\ v, #]]}&)\)[
          \((If[#3 \[NotEqual] 0, w, #1\ u + #2\ v + w]&)\)@@CL[l]]; \)\)], 
  "Input",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Drawing a circle given the center ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(p\)]],
  " and a point ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(q\)]],
  " on the circle."
}], "Text",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\(Circ[p_, q_] := 
      Module[{l, m, n, qq, rr}, \n\t\tl = PE[p, q]; \n\t\t
        qq = \ XP[p, PE[l, z], q, \(-1\)]; \n\t\tm = Perp[qq, l]; \n\t\t
        n = l + m; \n\t\trr = PE[n, Perp[q, n]]; \n\t\t
        P2P[u + I\ v, u - I\ v, \ q, qq, rr]]; \)\)], "Input",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell[TextData[{
  "A ",
  StyleBox["test",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " for congruence of segments."
}], "Text",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(Cong[p_, q_, pp_, qq_] := 
      Module[{r, s, qqq, f}, \n\t\tr = PE[PE[p, q], z]; \n\t\t
        s = PE[PE[p, pp], z]; \n\t\tqqq = PE[PE[q, s], PE[pp, r]]; \n\t\t
        f = Circ[pp, qqq]; \n\t\tExpandAll[PD[f, qq\^2] == 0]]\)], "Input",
  InitializationCell->True]
}, Closed]]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Curves", "Section"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Some invariants", "Subsubsection",
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell["Hessian matrix for a curve", "Text",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True,
  FontWeight->"Bold"],

Cell["MHP[ff_] := Outer[PD[ff,#1 #2]&, {u,v,w}, {u,v,w}];", "Input",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell["Hessian matrix for an envelope", "Text",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True,
  FontWeight->"Bold"],

Cell["MHL[gg_] := Outer[PD[#1 #2, gg]&, {x,y,z}, {x,y,z}];", "Input",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Conics determined by several points or lines", "Subsubsection",
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(P2P[q__] := 
      Module[{mm, kk}, mm = MP[{q}]; 
        kk = Table[{mm\[LeftDoubleBracket]ii, 1\[RightDoubleBracket]\^2, 
              mm\[LeftDoubleBracket]ii, 1\[RightDoubleBracket]\ 
                mm\[LeftDoubleBracket]ii, 2\[RightDoubleBracket], 
              mm\[LeftDoubleBracket]ii, 2\[RightDoubleBracket]\^2, 
              mm\[LeftDoubleBracket]ii, 1\[RightDoubleBracket]\ 
                mm\[LeftDoubleBracket]ii, 3\[RightDoubleBracket], 
              mm\[LeftDoubleBracket]ii, 2\[RightDoubleBracket]\ 
                mm\[LeftDoubleBracket]ii, 3\[RightDoubleBracket], 
              mm\[LeftDoubleBracket]ii, 3\[RightDoubleBracket]\^2}, {ii, 1, 
              5}]; Collect[Det[Join[{Bxyz[2]}, kk]], {x, y, z}]]\)], "Input",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(P2L[q__] := 
      Module[{mm, kk}, mm = ML[{q}]; 
        kk = Table[{mm\[LeftDoubleBracket]ii, 1\[RightDoubleBracket]\^2, 
              mm\[LeftDoubleBracket]ii, 1\[RightDoubleBracket]\ 
                mm\[LeftDoubleBracket]ii, 2\[RightDoubleBracket], 
              mm\[LeftDoubleBracket]ii, 2\[RightDoubleBracket]\^2, 
              mm\[LeftDoubleBracket]ii, 1\[RightDoubleBracket]\ 
                mm\[LeftDoubleBracket]ii, 3\[RightDoubleBracket], 
              mm\[LeftDoubleBracket]ii, 2\[RightDoubleBracket]\ 
                mm\[LeftDoubleBracket]ii, 3\[RightDoubleBracket], 
              mm\[LeftDoubleBracket]ii, 3\[RightDoubleBracket]\^2}, {ii, 1, 
              5}]; Collect[Det[Join[{Buvw[2]}, kk]], {x, y, z}]]\)], "Input",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Cubics determined by several points or lines", "Subsubsection",
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell["\<\
P3P[q__] := Module[{mm,kk}, mm = MP[List[q]];
    kk = Table[Bxyz[3]/.Thread[{x,y,z}->(mm[[i]])],{i,1,9}];    
    Tidy[Det[Join[{Bxyz[3]},kk]]]]                         \
\>", "Input",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell["\<\
P3L[q__] := Module[{mm,kk}, mm = ML[List[q]];
    kk = Table[Buvw[3]/.Thread[{u,v,w}->(mm[[i]])],{i,1,9}];    
    Tidy[Det[Join[{Buvw[3]},kk]]]]                         \
\>", "Input",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["From curves to envelopes and back", "Subsubsection"],

Cell["\<\
ClearAll[Envel];

Envel[f_] := Module[{n, p, a, b, c, coef, eqn},
    n = DegP[f];
    p = a u + b v + c w;
    coef = CL[PD[f, p^(n-1)]] - {u,v,w};
    eqn = Eliminate[Append[coef,p]==0, {a, b, c}];
    If[Head[eqn] === Equal, 
    \tTidy[Expand[eqn[[1]]-eqn[[2]]]],\"Fail\"]];\
\>", "Input",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->False],

Cell["\<\
ClearAll[Curve];

Curve[g_] := Dual[Envel[Dual[g]]];\
\>", "Input",
  InitializationCell->True]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Conic tangents", "Subsubsection"],

Cell["\<\
ClearAll[ConicTangents];
ConicTangents[f_, p_] := Module[{sol, q1, q2, xx, yy, zz},
Off[Solve::\"svars\"]; 
sol = Solve[{f==0,PD[f,p]==0},{x,y,z}]/.{x->xx,y->yy,z->zz};
On[Solve::\"svars\"];
q1 = xx u + yy v + zz w/.sol[[1]];
q2 = xx u + yy v + zz w/.sol[[2]];
Map[Together,{Tidy[q1],Tidy[q2]}/.{xx->1,yy->1,zz->1},{2}]]\
\>", "Input",
  InitializationCell->True]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Rank of the Hessian", "Subsubsection"],

Cell["Rank[conic_] := 3 - Length[NullSpace[MHP[conic]]];", "Input",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->False]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Quasi-inverse of a matrix", "Subsubsection",
  Evaluatable->False,
  AspectRatioFixed->True],

Cell["\<\
A square matrix multiplied by its quasi-inverse gives the  \
determinant times the identity matrix\
\>", "Text",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True,
  FontWeight->"Bold"],

Cell["\<\
QuasiInverse[mm_] := Block[{min,dim}, dim = Length[mm];
\t min = Reverse[Transpose[Reverse[Minors[mm,dim-1]]]];
\t\t Table[(-1)^(i+j)min[[i,j]], {i,dim},{j,dim}]];\
\>", "Input",
  InitializationCell->True,
  AspectRatioFixed->True]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Conic crossratios", "Subsubsection"],

Cell["\<\
RP2[f_,p1_,p2_,p3_,p4_] := 
                RL[PD[f,p1],PE[p1,p2],PE[p1,p3],PE[p1,p4]];\
\>", "Input",
  InitializationCell->True],

Cell["\<\
RL2[g_,l1_,l2_,l3_,l4_] := 
                RP[PD[l1,g],PE[l1,l2],PE[l1,l3],PE[l1,l4]];\
\>", "Input",
  InitializationCell->True]
}, Closed]]
}, Closed]]
},
